1
00:00:01,710 --> 00:00:04,000
[♪ opening theme song playing]

2
00:01:30,010 --> 00:01:31,510
♪

3
00:01:34,090 --> 00:01:35,850
Hold on. What's this?

4
00:01:36,510 --> 00:01:37,850
That's Tanikaze.

5
00:01:37,930 --> 00:01:39,720
How did they get here?

6
00:01:49,650 --> 00:01:54,030
[Tsugai 1
and Tsugai 2 yelling]

7
00:01:54,110 --> 00:01:55,530
[BUNBUN] Everybody...

8
00:01:55,610 --> 00:01:57,450
-[all gasp]
-...get down!

9
00:01:57,530 --> 00:01:59,330
[Midori grunts]

10
00:02:05,880 --> 00:02:07,170
[rumbling]

11
00:02:09,500 --> 00:02:11,210
[Hagure whimpers]

12
00:02:11,300 --> 00:02:13,380
Another one? What is happening?

13
00:02:15,890 --> 00:02:16,930
What's that?

14
00:02:25,940 --> 00:02:27,310
[Midori sighs]

15
00:02:27,400 --> 00:02:29,190
[Tachikawa whimpering]

16
00:02:29,690 --> 00:02:31,900
[JIJIMARU] My!
That's one sturdy sack.

17
00:02:31,990 --> 00:02:33,860
[MIDORI] Mm-mm-mm!

18
00:02:34,200 --> 00:02:37,490
-What's going on?
-[BABAMARU] Tanikaze exploded.

19
00:02:37,570 --> 00:02:38,530
[Natsuki grunts]

20
00:02:43,500 --> 00:02:45,580
Akio! Bunbun!

21
00:02:45,670 --> 00:02:47,790
-[TSUGAI 1] One, two...
-[TSUGAI 2] Three, four...

22
00:02:47,880 --> 00:02:49,540
Akio isn't down here.

23
00:02:49,630 --> 00:02:51,000
He's gone?

24
00:02:51,090 --> 00:02:52,550
[SAKURAZAWA]
Well, he didn't blow up.

25
00:02:52,630 --> 00:02:54,760
His viscera would be
all over the walls.

26
00:02:54,840 --> 00:02:56,550
So he escaped?

27
00:02:57,010 --> 00:02:58,430
[SAKURAZAWA] Aw, man.

28
00:02:58,510 --> 00:03:00,970
Looks like I'm gonna need
a whole new infirmary.

29
00:03:01,060 --> 00:03:02,470
[JIJIMARU] We've been had.

30
00:03:02,560 --> 00:03:05,690
Daemons always prioritize
their master's safety.

31
00:03:05,770 --> 00:03:07,520
They took advantage of that.

32
00:03:07,600 --> 00:03:10,520
Uh? Wait, so because
I was in danger,

33
00:03:10,610 --> 00:03:12,360
Midori had to let go of Akio?

34
00:03:12,440 --> 00:03:14,320
[NATSUKI]
Midori did nothing wrong.

35
00:03:14,900 --> 00:03:17,110
He protected you,
just like he should.

36
00:03:17,200 --> 00:03:19,410
Show him love. He's a good boy.

37
00:03:19,490 --> 00:03:21,490
-[Midori moans]
-[Tachikawa chuckles]

38
00:03:21,580 --> 00:03:24,410
I saw something on it
before it blew.

39
00:03:24,500 --> 00:03:26,960
There was a slimy mold
growing on Tanikaze.

40
00:03:27,580 --> 00:03:31,590
Earlier, I saw the same stuff
on Yamakaze at the front gate.

41
00:03:31,670 --> 00:03:32,800
[Natsuki exhales]

42
00:03:32,880 --> 00:03:34,970
[BUNBUN] I think
it's some kind of parasite

43
00:03:35,050 --> 00:03:36,800
that makes its host explode.

44
00:03:36,880 --> 00:03:39,680
But I wasn't able to detect
the daemon responsible for it.

45
00:03:40,220 --> 00:03:41,720
So it isn't just mold.

46
00:03:41,810 --> 00:03:43,680
That must be only one part
of the daemon.

47
00:03:44,520 --> 00:03:46,310
[JIJIMARU]
It can split into pieces?

48
00:03:46,390 --> 00:03:48,770
So it's like Asuma's daemons.

49
00:03:48,850 --> 00:03:51,190
In that case,
when did they get infected?

50
00:03:51,270 --> 00:03:55,740
I don't know. Damn it all.
Who'd do something like this?

51
00:03:55,820 --> 00:03:58,780
Turning helpless relics
into suicide bombers.

52
00:03:58,860 --> 00:04:00,120
They're monsters.

53
00:04:01,240 --> 00:04:02,950
All right. Come on.

54
00:04:03,870 --> 00:04:05,290
We're finding Akio.

55
00:04:05,370 --> 00:04:06,960
[BABAMARU AND JIJIMARU]
Mm. Mm.

56
00:04:07,040 --> 00:04:09,250
Look over there! Pair off!

57
00:04:09,330 --> 00:04:12,670
Daemons are inclined to protect
their masters above all else,

58
00:04:12,750 --> 00:04:14,460
and they used that.

59
00:04:15,760 --> 00:04:17,170
[servant grunting]

60
00:04:17,260 --> 00:04:19,220
[NATSUKI]
I don't deny that's true.

61
00:04:21,300 --> 00:04:24,560
And yet,
did they do it to free him,

62
00:04:24,640 --> 00:04:27,020
or did they want Akio dead?

63
00:04:41,450 --> 00:04:42,620
♪

64
00:04:47,450 --> 00:04:49,000
[ASA] Tell me
your honest thoughts!

65
00:04:49,080 --> 00:04:51,540
Do you like
this picture or this one?

66
00:04:51,630 --> 00:04:53,380
Personally, I think
they both look great!

67
00:04:53,460 --> 00:04:54,920
[FEMALE DAEMON]
We're back from patrol!

68
00:04:58,090 --> 00:04:59,670
[ASA] Doggie!

69
00:04:59,760 --> 00:05:02,510
[MALE DAEMON] There were a few
police cars at the warehouse,

70
00:05:02,590 --> 00:05:03,930
but nothing major.

71
00:05:04,010 --> 00:05:06,430
It didn't seem like
anyone was freaking out.

72
00:05:06,510 --> 00:05:07,720
Yeah?

73
00:05:08,060 --> 00:05:10,100
The sword pervert slaughtered
a whole bunch of people,

74
00:05:10,190 --> 00:05:11,940
but no one's taken notice.

75
00:05:12,650 --> 00:05:15,360
Guess they have someone
to get rid of the bodies, too.

76
00:05:16,020 --> 00:05:19,400
Seems so.
Jin's daemons are much the same.

77
00:05:19,490 --> 00:05:21,110
He had called them "janitors."

78
00:05:21,200 --> 00:05:24,700
Jin? Oh. So you've
usually got him

79
00:05:24,780 --> 00:05:26,540
when things get too messy.

80
00:05:26,620 --> 00:05:28,120
I haven't seen his daemons yet.

81
00:05:28,200 --> 00:05:29,870
Guess I'd better be careful.

82
00:05:30,370 --> 00:05:32,080
I wouldn't wanna be next.

83
00:05:32,170 --> 00:05:33,540
Yes, indeed.

84
00:05:33,630 --> 00:05:35,040
Of course we have a cleaner.

85
00:05:35,130 --> 00:05:36,960
Any self-respecting
faction would.

86
00:05:37,500 --> 00:05:40,920
Say, for example,
Higashi Village's "gravedigger."

87
00:05:41,010 --> 00:05:42,720
[DERA] This old goat.

88
00:05:42,800 --> 00:05:44,890
How much shit
does he have on Hana?

89
00:05:44,970 --> 00:05:46,050
-[door opens]
-Hmm?

90
00:05:46,720 --> 00:05:49,640
I found their security room
and erased all their footage.

91
00:05:50,270 --> 00:05:53,310
Tell me, Tadera.
How are your driving skills?

92
00:05:53,390 --> 00:05:54,770
Decent enough.

93
00:05:55,110 --> 00:05:58,690
[ASUMA] That car belongs to me.
You may use it to get back home.

94
00:05:58,770 --> 00:05:59,860
[DERA] Uh?

95
00:05:59,940 --> 00:06:01,320
Hey, thanks for the ride.

96
00:06:02,030 --> 00:06:03,450
So did you bug this thing?

97
00:06:03,530 --> 00:06:04,950
Gonna tail me again?

98
00:06:05,030 --> 00:06:06,320
Certainly not.

99
00:06:06,410 --> 00:06:09,450
In fact, I'd like to apologize
for the other day.

100
00:06:09,830 --> 00:06:12,000
Jin was quite angry with me.

101
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:15,210
Trust it will not happen again.

102
00:06:15,290 --> 00:06:16,750
[DERA] Yeah, totally.

103
00:06:17,630 --> 00:06:19,420
Before Tadera gets away,

104
00:06:19,500 --> 00:06:21,550
is there any info
you can get off of him?

105
00:06:21,630 --> 00:06:22,920
I'm afraid not.

106
00:06:23,010 --> 00:06:24,590
He doesn't have
his own daemons with him,

107
00:06:24,680 --> 00:06:25,840
so there's nothing we can do.

108
00:06:26,930 --> 00:06:28,890
-[GONZO] Mm...
-[phone rings]

109
00:06:31,100 --> 00:06:33,350
[GONZO] Jin, son. I'm so sorry.

110
00:06:33,440 --> 00:06:34,940
I meant to come right back...

111
00:06:35,850 --> 00:06:36,900
What?

112
00:06:37,360 --> 00:06:41,070
The infirmary?
Is Dr. Sakurazawa okay?

113
00:06:41,740 --> 00:06:44,400
-I see. Find him.
-[call disconnects]

114
00:06:44,900 --> 00:06:48,070
Asuma, Asa, time for us to go.

115
00:06:48,160 --> 00:06:50,120
-It seems Akio escaped.
-[Asuma gasps]

116
00:06:50,200 --> 00:06:51,370
[both gasp]

117
00:06:51,450 --> 00:06:53,040
[Yuru grunts]

118
00:06:54,080 --> 00:06:56,500
He... got away?

119
00:06:56,580 --> 00:06:58,670
-[Right and Left grunt]
-[YURU] Him too?

120
00:06:58,750 --> 00:07:00,130
And just like that,

121
00:07:00,210 --> 00:07:02,550
our only lead
on Mom and Dad disappeared.

122
00:07:02,630 --> 00:07:04,720
-[Yuru grunting]
-What's going on?

123
00:07:04,800 --> 00:07:06,760
-Yuru! What's wrong?
-[DANJI (TSUGAI)] Yuru!

124
00:07:06,840 --> 00:07:09,220
-[Yuru breathes heavily]
-[DERA] Whoa, there!

125
00:07:09,300 --> 00:07:10,810
You okay, kid?

126
00:07:11,470 --> 00:07:12,890
He's running a fever.

127
00:07:12,970 --> 00:07:15,390
This isn't uncommon
after people leave the mountain

128
00:07:15,480 --> 00:07:16,560
for the first time.

129
00:07:16,640 --> 00:07:18,190
It's like a new world to them,

130
00:07:18,270 --> 00:07:20,610
with new viruses
and new bacteria.

131
00:07:20,690 --> 00:07:23,780
If that weren't enough,
he's barely had a break.

132
00:07:23,860 --> 00:07:26,400
He's been fighting nonstop
since we got here,

133
00:07:26,490 --> 00:07:28,570
leaving him constantly tense.

134
00:07:28,660 --> 00:07:30,820
His body must be
screaming at him.

135
00:07:31,620 --> 00:07:33,660
Let's get him to our infirmary.

136
00:07:33,750 --> 00:07:35,950
Can't. It is out of commission
right now.

137
00:07:36,040 --> 00:07:38,460
Just hold on. You'll be okay.

138
00:07:38,540 --> 00:07:39,420
Leave it to me.

139
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:41,630
I've seen this before.

140
00:07:41,710 --> 00:07:43,300
Your brother's gonna be fine.

141
00:07:43,920 --> 00:07:46,420
We just gotta lay low
for a bit at my pad.

142
00:07:46,760 --> 00:07:48,720
I'll contact you again
through Jin's bar.

143
00:07:48,800 --> 00:07:50,050
Just wait till then.

144
00:07:51,600 --> 00:07:52,890
♪

145
00:08:00,110 --> 00:08:01,020
[phone chimes]

146
00:08:11,660 --> 00:08:13,620
[Akai moans]

147
00:08:17,410 --> 00:08:18,620
[Asa sighs]

148
00:08:19,670 --> 00:08:21,960
That said, being betrayed

149
00:08:22,040 --> 00:08:25,050
by someone this close
really stings.

150
00:08:37,430 --> 00:08:38,480
[Asa chuckles]

151
00:08:47,690 --> 00:08:48,650
[Haruo exhales]

152
00:09:01,170 --> 00:09:03,380
[NATSUKI]
We need to expand our search.

153
00:09:03,460 --> 00:09:07,000
We'll send one team to the back
and another one to the annex.

154
00:09:07,090 --> 00:09:08,630
-[SERVANT] Master Jin!
-Uh?

155
00:09:08,720 --> 00:09:10,590
[NATSUKI]
Did you two have any luck?

156
00:09:10,670 --> 00:09:13,010
There's nothing to find.
His room's a bust.

157
00:09:13,090 --> 00:09:16,720
Listen up. If you locate Akio,
don't engage.

158
00:09:16,810 --> 00:09:18,930
Just alert us
as fast as you can.

159
00:09:19,020 --> 00:09:20,060
[ALL] Sir.

160
00:09:20,560 --> 00:09:23,190
He should be considered
an extremely dangerous target.

161
00:09:23,270 --> 00:09:26,440
As a rule, stay in groups
of two or more.

162
00:09:26,520 --> 00:09:29,990
No matter what,
don't ever find yourself alone.

163
00:09:30,070 --> 00:09:32,150
[servant grunting]

164
00:09:34,200 --> 00:09:36,490
-[servant choking]
-[Tsugai growling]

165
00:09:58,390 --> 00:10:01,180
[AKIO] Sorry, little guys.
You're strays now.

166
00:10:01,850 --> 00:10:04,690
Well, I'm sure you'll be found
before long.

167
00:10:09,820 --> 00:10:10,940
Uh?

168
00:10:12,070 --> 00:10:13,860
♪

169
00:10:19,370 --> 00:10:20,620
[sighs]

170
00:10:32,050 --> 00:10:33,920
[HANA]
It's not bleeding anymore.

171
00:10:34,010 --> 00:10:36,890
All we do is wait for the skin
to heal on its own.

172
00:10:37,470 --> 00:10:39,010
Did he ever get a tetanus shot?

173
00:10:39,100 --> 00:10:40,890
Every kid in Higashi did.

174
00:10:40,970 --> 00:10:42,850
The late shaman
took care of that.

175
00:10:43,640 --> 00:10:45,690
I fixed up an ice pack
if you want one.

176
00:10:45,770 --> 00:10:46,980
[HANA] Thanks, Ken.

177
00:10:48,270 --> 00:10:49,480
[Yuru grunts]

178
00:10:49,570 --> 00:10:51,690
[HANA] Now you need to get
some shut eye.

179
00:10:51,780 --> 00:10:53,820
It's not too cold
on your neck, right?

180
00:10:54,150 --> 00:10:55,610
No, it's good.

181
00:10:55,700 --> 00:10:57,070
Sorry for the trouble.

182
00:10:57,160 --> 00:10:58,370
When you're this sick,

183
00:10:58,700 --> 00:11:00,740
you shouldn't be worried
about any dumb crap like that.

184
00:11:00,830 --> 00:11:03,540
We've all gotta help our friends
when they're in need.

185
00:11:03,620 --> 00:11:04,870
Those aliens...

186
00:11:04,960 --> 00:11:07,170
or rather, the daemons
in black had said that.

187
00:11:07,790 --> 00:11:10,710
"We're all the same.
None of us can live alone."

188
00:11:11,500 --> 00:11:12,800
[Yuru groans]

189
00:11:13,510 --> 00:11:15,420
Thank you, Ken.

190
00:11:15,510 --> 00:11:16,880
The next time you're sick,

191
00:11:16,970 --> 00:11:19,550
I'll hunt a boar and cook up
some stew just for you.

192
00:11:19,640 --> 00:11:20,640
[KEN] Mm...

193
00:11:21,260 --> 00:11:23,560
Please keep your care-giving
within the bounds of the law!

194
00:11:23,640 --> 00:11:25,980
Should we be in fear
for his life?

195
00:11:26,060 --> 00:11:27,230
With us by his side,

196
00:11:27,310 --> 00:11:29,270
he should make it
through this A-okay.

197
00:11:29,940 --> 00:11:32,820
I'm sorry for worrying you.
I'll be fine.

198
00:11:33,190 --> 00:11:34,150
[Ken grunts]

199
00:11:34,820 --> 00:11:37,650
Now what do you think
you're apologizing for, lad?

200
00:11:37,740 --> 00:11:39,160
Just rest and get better!

201
00:11:39,240 --> 00:11:41,990
Then our hunt for the pervert
may continue!

202
00:11:42,080 --> 00:11:43,240
[Yuru groans, chuckles]

203
00:11:43,330 --> 00:11:46,710
Your hand's cool.
The soft stone feels nice.

204
00:11:46,790 --> 00:11:48,000
[RIGHT] Uh?

205
00:11:48,080 --> 00:11:50,750
-Oh, really?
-'Tis only logical.

206
00:11:50,840 --> 00:11:53,800
[RIGHT] Very well!
Take these to fight your fever!

207
00:11:53,880 --> 00:11:55,550
-[thuds]
-[Yuru groans]

208
00:11:56,550 --> 00:11:58,630
I think I'll pass, actually.

209
00:12:00,760 --> 00:12:02,720
[HANA] Some sleep
will be good for you.

210
00:12:02,800 --> 00:12:04,100
Night-night.

211
00:12:05,270 --> 00:12:08,600
And with that out of the way,
I don't even know

212
00:12:08,690 --> 00:12:11,060
where I'm supposed to start
with the rest of you guys.

213
00:12:11,150 --> 00:12:13,020
Another secret love child?

214
00:12:13,110 --> 00:12:14,980
She's just a child
from Higashi Village

215
00:12:15,070 --> 00:12:16,280
who was kidnapped.

216
00:12:16,360 --> 00:12:18,360
[HANA] You can't have
an actual dog in here.

217
00:12:18,450 --> 00:12:20,200
The building doesn't allow pets.

218
00:12:20,280 --> 00:12:22,280
[DERA] He's a Daemon Wielder.

219
00:12:22,370 --> 00:12:26,620
[BOTH] This perfect specimen...
is our beloved master!

220
00:12:26,700 --> 00:12:28,250
[HANA] Leave Earth in peace.

221
00:12:28,330 --> 00:12:30,420
You're Zashiki-Warashi, right?

222
00:12:30,500 --> 00:12:32,380
Legends say you bring
good fortune to homes.

223
00:12:32,460 --> 00:12:34,290
Please enjoy your stay.

224
00:12:34,710 --> 00:12:35,960
May I give you a seat?

225
00:12:36,050 --> 00:12:37,760
[BOTH] Double-standard!

226
00:12:37,840 --> 00:12:40,050
[Oshirasama, in sing-song voice]
I'm back!

227
00:12:40,130 --> 00:12:42,260
It seems we found
quite the party!

228
00:12:42,350 --> 00:12:43,430
[both exclaim]

229
00:12:43,510 --> 00:12:44,760
Your small apartment

230
00:12:44,850 --> 00:12:47,060
is turning into a real clubhouse
for daemons.

231
00:12:47,140 --> 00:12:49,180
Not to suggest
we don't want you to join us,

232
00:12:49,270 --> 00:12:50,730
but didn't you go home?

233
00:12:50,810 --> 00:12:51,810
[Oshirasama chuckles]

234
00:12:52,360 --> 00:12:54,900
We went sightseeing in Tokyo!

235
00:12:54,980 --> 00:12:56,990
Looks like you had
a real fun time.

236
00:12:57,070 --> 00:12:58,240
[OSHIRASAMA] I did,

237
00:12:58,320 --> 00:13:00,150
and I got enough souvenirs
for everyone.

238
00:13:00,860 --> 00:13:03,910
[HANA] Hold on, you have
human money on you?

239
00:13:03,990 --> 00:13:06,870
Wait. Did you make yourself
visible to shop?

240
00:13:06,950 --> 00:13:08,620
[OSHIRASAMA]
We just talked to seers.

241
00:13:08,710 --> 00:13:11,210
Temples and shrines
are full of them!

242
00:13:11,290 --> 00:13:13,460
Our new friends gave us
lots of knickknacks!

243
00:13:13,540 --> 00:13:16,090
Oh, my! You're new here.

244
00:13:16,170 --> 00:13:18,340
You must be little Danji's
other half!

245
00:13:18,420 --> 00:13:19,590
This is Oshirasama.

246
00:13:20,090 --> 00:13:21,340
Good evening.

247
00:13:21,760 --> 00:13:24,510
[OSHIRASAMA] And this one...
Is she a girl from the village?

248
00:13:24,600 --> 00:13:28,350
Oh, what a sweetheart!
I simply love children!

249
00:13:28,430 --> 00:13:30,930
Oh, right, she can't see us.

250
00:13:31,020 --> 00:13:32,060
[AZAMI] Uh?

251
00:13:32,140 --> 00:13:33,350
Hi there.

252
00:13:33,440 --> 00:13:35,730
-I'm Oshirasama!
-[Azami groans]

253
00:13:35,820 --> 00:13:37,860
[DERA] Uh-oh!
She's goin' down again!

254
00:13:38,990 --> 00:13:41,650
Here. Would you take care
of this for me?

255
00:13:41,740 --> 00:13:42,860
[Azami gasps softly]

256
00:13:47,160 --> 00:13:48,540
Thank you, miss.

257
00:13:48,620 --> 00:13:49,830
[BOTH] She won her over!

258
00:13:50,330 --> 00:13:53,880
[cries] So, uh, some scary guys
attacked the village.

259
00:13:53,960 --> 00:13:56,290
The bad people killed my mommy.

260
00:13:56,380 --> 00:13:57,790
It was awful.

261
00:13:57,880 --> 00:14:02,220
Oh! That must have been hard.
You're so brave, dear.

262
00:14:02,300 --> 00:14:05,390
Whoa! She got the kid
to open up in no time at all.

263
00:14:05,470 --> 00:14:06,720
There was a girl.

264
00:14:06,800 --> 00:14:08,350
And even though
she had cute braids

265
00:14:08,430 --> 00:14:10,850
and a red outfit,
her face looked mean.

266
00:14:10,930 --> 00:14:14,020
She moved her hands,
and the adults split in half.

267
00:14:14,480 --> 00:14:15,900
And that's how Mommy...

268
00:14:15,980 --> 00:14:18,150
Would this be the girl
with the denture daemons

269
00:14:18,230 --> 00:14:19,690
you mentioned a while ago?

270
00:14:19,780 --> 00:14:23,740
Yep. Some pipsqueak named Gabby
and her chompy friends.

271
00:14:24,990 --> 00:14:26,320
The way Asa was talking,

272
00:14:26,410 --> 00:14:28,780
it seems like the Kagemoris
take good care of her.

273
00:14:28,870 --> 00:14:30,870
But they still killed
Azami's ma.

274
00:14:30,950 --> 00:14:33,160
We can't just force her
to stay with them.

275
00:14:33,540 --> 00:14:34,750
Though if she goes back,

276
00:14:34,830 --> 00:14:36,250
Higashi might
throw her in a cell

277
00:14:36,330 --> 00:14:37,880
because she's seen too much!

278
00:14:37,960 --> 00:14:39,000
No way!

279
00:14:39,090 --> 00:14:41,670
Please, will you keep Azami
safe here?

280
00:14:41,760 --> 00:14:44,420
[Hana stutters] Aw, what?

281
00:14:44,510 --> 00:14:46,300
Why is it every time
you leave the house,

282
00:14:46,380 --> 00:14:48,850
you come back with a new kid
we need to take care of?

283
00:14:48,930 --> 00:14:50,390
I mean, it kind of makes sense.

284
00:14:50,470 --> 00:14:52,520
Won't she feel better in a place
with people she knows,

285
00:14:52,600 --> 00:14:53,520
like Yuru and me?

286
00:14:54,020 --> 00:14:55,600
[HANA] And how
do you think we can afford

287
00:14:55,690 --> 00:14:57,110
a whole another child?

288
00:14:57,190 --> 00:14:58,440
Or did you forget,

289
00:14:58,730 --> 00:15:00,650
you might never get any work
from Higashi Village again

290
00:15:00,730 --> 00:15:03,360
after your little falling out
with the bandits the other day.

291
00:15:03,440 --> 00:15:05,860
I wonder when
the next G-one race happens.

292
00:15:05,950 --> 00:15:06,990
-[chuckles]
-[Hana grunts]

293
00:15:07,070 --> 00:15:09,200
You are not gambling
our money away!

294
00:15:09,280 --> 00:15:10,700
It's not gambling if I win.

295
00:15:10,780 --> 00:15:13,160
It'll happen this time,
I promise.

296
00:15:13,250 --> 00:15:14,620
[Azami cries]

297
00:15:14,710 --> 00:15:15,910
[KIRI (TSUGAI)] It'll be okay.

298
00:15:16,000 --> 00:15:17,750
[DANJI (TSUGAI)]
We're here for you.

299
00:15:17,830 --> 00:15:19,170
I want to go home.

300
00:15:19,250 --> 00:15:20,540
[OSHIRASAMA]
On the bullet train?

301
00:15:20,630 --> 00:15:22,800
Or on the highway? Horseback?

302
00:15:22,880 --> 00:15:24,420
[Azami continues crying]

303
00:15:25,380 --> 00:15:28,590
[overlapping chatter]

304
00:15:28,680 --> 00:15:30,260
[MALE DAEMON] You can do it.

305
00:15:30,350 --> 00:15:31,510
[indistinct chatter]

306
00:15:31,600 --> 00:15:33,390
[KEN] A sick person's
trying to sleep.

307
00:15:33,470 --> 00:15:37,020
Keep it down.
This just confirms what I knew.

308
00:15:37,100 --> 00:15:39,440
I'm the only normal one here.

309
00:15:40,730 --> 00:15:41,940
I'm so sorry.

310
00:15:42,020 --> 00:15:43,860
How are you supposed
to get any rest like this?

311
00:15:43,940 --> 00:15:44,940
[gasps]

312
00:15:46,200 --> 00:15:48,950
What? Where'd Yuru go?

313
00:15:49,030 --> 00:15:51,490
How could he have left
if he's too sick to walk?

314
00:15:51,580 --> 00:15:53,540
He hasn't strayed too far, lad.

315
00:15:56,410 --> 00:15:57,500
[YURU] I'm in here.

316
00:15:57,580 --> 00:15:58,920
[screams]

317
00:15:59,000 --> 00:16:01,380
What are you doing
stuffed inside your closet?

318
00:16:01,460 --> 00:16:03,300
Get your little butt back to bed
this instant.

319
00:16:03,380 --> 00:16:05,300
No, thanks. I'm comfortable.

320
00:16:06,010 --> 00:16:08,180
Small, dark places
help me feel relaxed

321
00:16:08,260 --> 00:16:09,630
when I'm too sick to fight.

322
00:16:09,720 --> 00:16:11,760
What are you, a wild animal?

323
00:16:11,850 --> 00:16:13,560
Quite the opposite of Asa.

324
00:16:14,140 --> 00:16:15,600
[HANA] So, what do you think?

325
00:16:15,680 --> 00:16:17,930
-Are you well enough to eat?
-[Yuru groans]

326
00:16:18,020 --> 00:16:20,560
-[HANA] How about some rice?
-Yes, please.

327
00:16:20,650 --> 00:16:22,320
All right. [chuckles]

328
00:16:29,280 --> 00:16:30,660
That's the stuff.

329
00:16:30,740 --> 00:16:33,410
I don't know how you do it,
but these are amazing!

330
00:16:33,490 --> 00:16:34,780
Aw, you flatter me.

331
00:16:34,870 --> 00:16:37,710
When you're done with those,
try taking these.

332
00:16:37,790 --> 00:16:39,920
[YURU] Huh?
What are these pebbles?

333
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:41,420
[DERA] Analgesic antipyretics.

334
00:16:41,500 --> 00:16:43,880
Mm. If I'm already
not feeling well,

335
00:16:43,960 --> 00:16:45,960
why would I eat
some strange little rocks?

336
00:16:46,050 --> 00:16:47,470
[DERA] You'll be fine.

337
00:16:47,550 --> 00:16:50,090
The people up in the village
take these all the time.

338
00:16:50,630 --> 00:16:53,390
It's the medicinal painkiller
I used to bring you guys

339
00:16:53,470 --> 00:16:55,010
from the outside world.

340
00:16:55,100 --> 00:16:57,100
I ground them up
so they'd look kind of special,

341
00:16:57,180 --> 00:16:59,140
but you can buy them
at any corner store.

342
00:16:59,230 --> 00:17:00,980
[YURU]
The medicine's that common?

343
00:17:01,060 --> 00:17:03,150
[DERA] Yep, these things
are mass-produced

344
00:17:03,230 --> 00:17:05,150
-by some machines.
-Uh, in the village,

345
00:17:05,230 --> 00:17:07,980
people would talk about this
like it's a miracle cure.

346
00:17:08,070 --> 00:17:09,650
I figured it was
a luxury product

347
00:17:09,740 --> 00:17:11,490
made by some master healer.

348
00:17:11,570 --> 00:17:13,700
[chuckles] It gets the job done.

349
00:17:13,780 --> 00:17:15,530
[YURU] Umm...

350
00:17:16,040 --> 00:17:17,080
♪

351
00:17:18,580 --> 00:17:20,160
[Yuru breathes shakily]

352
00:17:25,090 --> 00:17:26,300
[Yuru grunts]

353
00:17:32,680 --> 00:17:34,180
[DERA] I told you
to finish eating

354
00:17:34,260 --> 00:17:35,390
before you took it.

355
00:17:35,470 --> 00:17:37,430
But hey, at least
your appetite's back

356
00:17:37,520 --> 00:17:38,770
with a vengeance.

357
00:17:38,850 --> 00:17:40,480
-[HANA] Hmm.
-[Yuru grunting]

358
00:17:40,890 --> 00:17:41,980
[KEN] Uh?

359
00:17:43,650 --> 00:17:45,060
[Right chuckles]

360
00:17:53,860 --> 00:17:56,700
[OSHIRASAMA] Isn't this
a beautiful view, darling?

361
00:17:56,780 --> 00:17:57,790
[horse neighs]

362
00:17:58,200 --> 00:18:00,080
[HANA] Of course,
right as my husband's income

363
00:18:00,160 --> 00:18:01,290
is about to tank,

364
00:18:01,580 --> 00:18:04,210
I somehow get stuck
with another little brat.

365
00:18:04,290 --> 00:18:05,880
To make matters worse,

366
00:18:05,960 --> 00:18:07,590
two of our kids
aren't even registered.

367
00:18:08,710 --> 00:18:11,010
What a pain in the frigging ass.

368
00:18:11,090 --> 00:18:13,010
Eh, we'll figure it out somehow.

369
00:18:13,090 --> 00:18:15,340
I don't get how
you're so chill about this.

370
00:18:15,430 --> 00:18:17,510
Where does all that
composure come from?

371
00:18:17,600 --> 00:18:20,350
What? Like it's hard
staying cool as a king

372
00:18:20,430 --> 00:18:22,350
when I know a queen like you
has my back

373
00:18:22,430 --> 00:18:24,100
-no matter what happens?
-[sighs]

374
00:18:26,310 --> 00:18:28,860
So, queen.
You team "Yuru should die?"

375
00:18:28,940 --> 00:18:30,980
It's no secret
I don't like kids.

376
00:18:31,070 --> 00:18:33,280
But I am firmly on team
"adults who trample

377
00:18:33,360 --> 00:18:35,780
over the lives of innocent kids
should die."

378
00:18:37,410 --> 00:18:38,870
[Dera chuckles]

379
00:18:38,950 --> 00:18:40,330
♪

380
00:18:42,910 --> 00:18:46,290
Whew-ie! We've had
a productive day, kiddos!

381
00:18:46,380 --> 00:18:48,380
Time to wash up
and say goodnight.

382
00:18:48,460 --> 00:18:50,000
If you share a room with Yuru,

383
00:18:50,090 --> 00:18:51,630
you might catch
whatever bug he's got.

384
00:18:51,710 --> 00:18:53,720
How about you crash with me
tonight, Ken?

385
00:18:53,800 --> 00:18:54,760
Sounds good.

386
00:18:55,130 --> 00:18:57,010
You'll be staying with me
in my room, Azami.

387
00:18:57,090 --> 00:18:59,010
[AZAMI] Uh? [groans]

388
00:18:59,100 --> 00:19:01,390
This young lady's
gonna take care of you!

389
00:19:01,470 --> 00:19:03,930
She's not scary, I promise.

390
00:19:05,140 --> 00:19:06,140
♪

391
00:19:06,230 --> 00:19:08,690
[Hana breathes deeply]

392
00:19:10,190 --> 00:19:13,070
[snores, chuckles]

393
00:19:13,150 --> 00:19:15,570
[Dera snoring]

394
00:19:21,200 --> 00:19:23,580
[Ken and Azami whimpering]

395
00:19:23,660 --> 00:19:26,580
[BOTH] This room is terrifying.

396
00:19:27,170 --> 00:19:29,880
-[footsteps]
-[siren wailing distantly]

397
00:19:37,090 --> 00:19:39,430
-[MINASE] Oh, there you are.
-[Akio grunts]

398
00:19:43,180 --> 00:19:45,270
I've been waiting, Akio.

399
00:19:45,890 --> 00:19:46,940
[exclaims]

400
00:19:47,440 --> 00:19:50,310
-Hey, Mom, you're here.
-[Minase gasps]

401
00:19:50,400 --> 00:19:53,860
-What happened to you?
-I'm okay.

402
00:19:53,940 --> 00:19:57,990
No, you're clearly not okay!
And you're pale as a ghost!

403
00:19:58,070 --> 00:19:59,780
I lost a little blood.

404
00:20:00,320 --> 00:20:02,660
I think I need some rest.

405
00:20:03,040 --> 00:20:04,660
Forgive me, son.

406
00:20:04,740 --> 00:20:07,370
I should have come
to save you myself.

407
00:20:07,710 --> 00:20:10,000
I never would have let
something so awful

408
00:20:10,080 --> 00:20:11,460
happen to my baby.

409
00:20:12,130 --> 00:20:14,420
[AKIO] Thank you, Mom.

410
00:20:14,840 --> 00:20:17,670
[MINASE] But now,
I'm never letting you go.

411
00:20:17,760 --> 00:20:19,800
Never, Akio.

412
00:20:20,640 --> 00:20:21,640
[AKIO] Hm.

413
00:20:22,140 --> 00:20:23,930
♪

414
00:20:24,770 --> 00:20:26,270
[MISASAGI]
The ties of one's blood

415
00:20:26,350 --> 00:20:27,930
are nothing but a curse.

416
00:20:28,350 --> 00:20:31,020
No matter how hard
we might try to fight it,

417
00:20:31,110 --> 00:20:33,360
we can't escape that truth.

418
00:20:34,150 --> 00:20:35,860
Got some context there?

419
00:20:35,940 --> 00:20:38,110
[MISASAGI]
We've recovered Akio alive.

420
00:20:38,190 --> 00:20:41,320
Recovered! Recovered! Recovered!

421
00:20:41,410 --> 00:20:44,240
I'm impressed!
I thought he was dead meat.

422
00:20:44,330 --> 00:20:47,120
My apologies. I guess
I missed him with my blast.

423
00:20:47,200 --> 00:20:50,710
Bah! I'm sure we can find
some way we can use him.

424
00:20:51,250 --> 00:20:54,710
Now then, I wonder how much
of our information

425
00:20:54,800 --> 00:20:55,840
leaked to Jin's guys.

426
00:20:56,760 --> 00:20:57,880
With a little luck,

427
00:20:57,960 --> 00:20:59,590
the Kagemoris
and Higashi Village

428
00:20:59,670 --> 00:21:01,630
will keep tearing each other
limb from limb.

429
00:21:01,720 --> 00:21:04,220
I hope so.
Ivan even managed to kill

430
00:21:04,310 --> 00:21:06,020
a bunch of
Higashi Village fighters.

431
00:21:06,100 --> 00:21:09,520
Limb from limb!
Limb from limb! Limb from limb!

432
00:21:10,310 --> 00:21:11,980
[BUNBUN] Oh, I just remembered.

433
00:21:12,060 --> 00:21:15,150
A while back,
I think I heard about a mold.

434
00:21:15,230 --> 00:21:17,190
There was a story
from my homeland.

435
00:21:17,280 --> 00:21:19,360
You're not from around here?

436
00:21:19,440 --> 00:21:22,200
[BUNBUN] My ancestors were
from Tottori prefecture.

437
00:21:22,700 --> 00:21:24,830
If I'm remembering
the story correctly,

438
00:21:24,910 --> 00:21:26,450
there's a daemon
from Western Japan

439
00:21:26,540 --> 00:21:27,830
that attaches to relics.

440
00:21:27,910 --> 00:21:29,910
And they sprout
some kind of slime-mold.

441
00:21:30,000 --> 00:21:31,790
-[both grunt]
-[BUNBUN] It's gotta be.

442
00:21:31,870 --> 00:21:35,500
I did see it. It was that daemon
from out West.

443
00:21:35,590 --> 00:21:38,010
It's been 400 long years.

444
00:21:39,130 --> 00:21:42,510
We can't miss our opportunity
to set matters right.

445
00:21:45,180 --> 00:21:49,180
And this war
will belong to the West.

446
00:21:49,270 --> 00:21:50,770
♪

447
00:21:55,020 --> 00:21:57,400
[♪ closing theme song playing]

448
00:23:28,070 --> 00:23:29,490
[ASA] He was a normal man

449
00:23:29,580 --> 00:23:31,790
who didn't wish death
on anybody.

450
00:23:31,870 --> 00:23:34,080
He was just trying
to live his life!

451
00:23:34,160 --> 00:23:35,540
[YURU] Do you want me
to go with you

452
00:23:35,620 --> 00:23:36,920
and teach 'em all a lesson?
